<odoo noupdate="1">
<!-- Three-Color Academic Warning System default levels (Bab 8.3 of the
     YPII Guideline). The Python Code below reproduces the guideline's own
     example trigger (count of subjects below the passing grade), but any
     school unit is free to edit these records (or add new ones) with a
     different formula since the evaluation is entirely data-driven -
     school_academic_alert._evaluate_alert_level() never hard-codes it.
     Levels are evaluated from the highest sequence down (most severe
     first), so Red (30) is checked before Orange (20) before Yellow (10). -->
<record id="school_academic_alert_level_yellow" model="school_academic_alert_level">
    <field name="name">Yellow - Early Warning</field>
    <field name="code">ALERT-LEVEL-YELLOW</field>
    <field name="color">yellow</field>
    <field name="sequence">10</field>
    <field name="python_code">result = trigger_count >= 2</field>
    <field
            name="action_guideline"
        >Homeroom Teacher informs the parent informally (e.g. via WhatsApp) that the student is showing early signs of academic difficulty in 2 or more subjects, and offers guidance/remedial support.</field>
    <field
            name="sla_text"
        >Parent informed within 3 school days of the alert being raised.</field>
</record>

<record id="school_academic_alert_level_orange" model="school_academic_alert_level">
    <field name="name">Orange - Serious Warning</field>
    <field name="code">ALERT-LEVEL-ORANGE</field>
    <field name="color">orange</field>
    <field name="sequence">20</field>
    <field name="python_code">result = trigger_count >= 3</field>
    <field
            name="action_guideline"
        >Counselor/Vice Principal schedules a formal meeting with the parent to discuss a remedial plan for the student, who is now below the passing grade in 3 or more subjects. A School Incident may be created to track follow-up.</field>
    <field
            name="sla_text"
        >Parent meeting scheduled within 5 school days of the alert being raised.</field>
</record>

<record id="school_academic_alert_level_red" model="school_academic_alert_level">
    <field name="name">Red - Critical Warning</field>
    <field name="code">ALERT-LEVEL-RED</field>
    <field name="color">red</field>
    <field name="sequence">30</field>
    <field name="python_code">result = trigger_count >= 4</field>
    <field
            name="action_guideline"
        >Principal is notified and a School Incident is created immediately; the student is below the passing grade in 4 or more subjects and is at risk of not being promoted. A joint remedial plan with the parent is mandatory.</field>
    <field
            name="sla_text"
        >Principal-level meeting held within 2 school days of the alert being raised.</field>
</record>
</odoo>
